			{
				"type": "Comment",
				"start": 0,
				"end": 434,
				"data": "\n\tThe follower never turns a space into a newline either: a space before a COMMENT, a\n\t`{@debug}` or a control-flow block that renders inline is that follower's own per-width wrap\n\tafter any sibling, exactly as it already is after text — a comment's line is authorship, and\n\tit is the NEWLINE spelling that holds it. Prettier keeps the space after text and breaks it\n\twith the container after an element, a component or a tag.\n"
			},
